WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
The first time we were hearing

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.769
directly from China.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.637
After surprising reports

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.072
that a suspected Chinese

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.974
spy balloon is floating over

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.209
the northern U.S.,

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.377
the Chinese foreign ministry

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.312
spokesperson addressed the situation

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.446
a short time ago,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.115
saying they are aware of the reports.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.649
And we'll have more on a live report

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.385
from Beijing in just a moment.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:19.953
But a senior US defense

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.388
official says the Pentagon

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.288
is confident

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.123
this surveillance

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.392
balloon belongs to China.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:25.892
The U.S.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.460
has been tracking it for a few days

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.662
and it has entered Montana via Canada.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:30.597
We've been hearing

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.999
that it does not pose a serious risk,

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.335
but it is traveling near sensitive sites.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.036
And people

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.037
living in the Billings,

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.638
Montana area definitely noticed

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.340
something strange in the sky.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.341
Less and less

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.477
is the moon

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.849
and

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.751
there's that

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.890
What planet is that?

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.491
Okay.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.260
That's the moon.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.461
It's a little fuzzy out here.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.862
And it's a kind of a credit phone,

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.098
but it's slightly overcast.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.534
But what the heck is that?

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.969
That's not the sun.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.939
And according to my little planet guide,

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.109
it's not a planet.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.710
What the heck is that?

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.948
Any help would be appreciated.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.217
The military and White House

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.251
say there are no plans

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.653
to shoot down the balloon.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.721
It's traveling at a very high altitude,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.590
well above commercial air traffic.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.791
But the balloon is near

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.826
a potential target

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.627
for Chinese espionage,

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.663
intercontinental ballistic missiles

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:39.032
located in Montana.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.300
Meanwhile, the Biden administration

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.801
says it acted immediately

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.769
to prevent the balloon

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:43.470
from collecting

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.271
any sensitive information.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.039
CNN's Pentagon

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:46.773
correspondent Oren

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.641
Liebermann picks up the story.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.643
It will say it came into the U.S.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.812
over Montana coming in from Canada.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.546
And that's

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.781
where they began tracking it

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.816
at first launching F-22 fighter jets.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:57.517
In the end,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.518
the decision was made

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.186
not to shoot it down.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:00.753
President Joe

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.789
Biden was asked for military options,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.524
but senior military leaders,

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.492
including chairman of the Joint

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.726
Chiefs, General Mark Milley,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.928
advised against shooting this down.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.597
Instead, they are keeping an eye on it

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.031
and seeing where it goes.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.233
The Pentagon does acknowledge

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.234
this traveled over

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.902
several sensitive sites,

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:16.970
though they won't specify

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.238
which sites those are.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.206
It is worth noting that Montana is home

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.341
to ballistic missile silos.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:23.776
So perhaps that's what this was after.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.545
It is also worth noting, of course,

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.312
that the Pentagon says

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.147
they are confident,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.548
very confident, in fact,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.183
that this was launched by China

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.251
and they brought it up through

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.185
diplomatic channels

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.586
both here in Washington

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.854
and in Beijing,

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.923
essentially to express how angry they are

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:37.557
about this

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:39.859
Well,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.828
CNN Beijing bureau chief Steven

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.029
Jiang joins me now.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:43.630
And Stephen,

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.131
we just got reaction

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.666
from Beijing to this.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.401
What are they saying

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:50.537
Yeah, can

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.604
I just

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.072
came back from the Foreign Ministry's

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:53.706
daily briefing

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.874
where I asked them

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:55.642
three questions

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.510
about this alleged Chinese spy balloon.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.212
What's interesting is disposal

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:01.347
did not deny the balloon belongs

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.549
to China outright.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.249
Instead,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.552
she gave this rather vague answer,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.886
as you can see on your screen.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.320
She said,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.455
we are aware of reports of the balloon

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.223
and are trying

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:10.857
to understand

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.425
the circumstances and verify

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.327
the details of the situation.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.161
I'd like to stress

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.829
that before it becomes clear

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.597
what happened.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.866
Any deliberate speculation or hyping up

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.568
what now would not help

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.670
the handling of the matter, she added.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.939
China is a responsible country.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.173
We act in accordance

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.441
with international law

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:29.742
and we have no intention

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.744
of violating our country's airspace.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.612
We hope relevant

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.113
parties will handle the matter

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.715
in a cool handed way.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.549
So this

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.384
rather muted response

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.719
seemed to give some credence

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.486
to the analysis

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:40.853
by some

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.621
US experts

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.257
that the revelation of this balloon

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.959
was deliberate on the part

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.893
of some of US officials

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.028
to really put the Chinese on the backfoot

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.630
ahead of the uplink and visit

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.131
to allow the Secretary

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.466
to really addressed

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.568
this issue with them more directly,

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.569
to confront them,

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.437
to basically

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:57.837
tell them

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:58.805
what the US knows

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.640
and what the US would like to see

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.741
Chinese do.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.976
But it's also interesting

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.744
that when I and other reporters

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.845
asked the Foreign Ministry

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.848
spokeswoman about if this revelation

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.017
would have any impact on this planned

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.085
high stakes visit,

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.386
she dodged the question

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.288
simply saying she has no information

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:16.589
or updates to announce.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.091
But the timing of this of course, is

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.093
what makes this very delicate

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:20.994
and also

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.062
potentially highly consequential,

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.064
because it really complicates things

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:25.732
at a time

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.900
when both governments, at least publicly,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.368
are saying

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.535
they're trying to reset

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.637
or at least stabilize

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:31.838
this increasingly contentious

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.639
relationship.

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:33.172
And remember,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.341
this kind of incident incidents really

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.242
in a way playing

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.478
to the hands of hardliners on both sides.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:38.845
Already,

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:39.712
we are seeing

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.482
some members of Congress in Washington

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.317
calling for stronger actions

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.218
and new briefings

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.153
and in portraying this as yet

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:48.488
another example

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.922
of how President

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.625
Biden's China policy is being too weak.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.294
And similarly, on the Chinese sides,

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:54.927
you could see this

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.829
potentially really stir

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.765
up more nationalistic sentiment

00:04:58.765 --> 00:04:59.532
and feelings.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:00.333
And so,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:00.667
you know,

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.602
this obviously is not happening

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.603
in a vacuum.

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.504
Ahead of this visit,

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.673
we are already seeing a flurry of

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:08.474
activities on the US part,

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.042
not only on

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.643
the economic and technology front,

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:12.478
but also in the military sphere

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:13.012
in terms

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.682
of shoring up its presence in the region,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:16.983
including those newly

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.418
signed agreements with the Philippines

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.586
and even without this balloon revelation.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:21.888
Expectations already

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:23.890
very low about this visit in terms

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.691
concrete results

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.526
out of the meetings between Blinken

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:28.561
and his Chinese counterpart, Kim.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.096
And with this revelation,

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.231
I think it's just adding more uncertainty

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:32.899
to this trip.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:33.666
For more on this,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.701
I want to bring in Malcolm

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.369
Davis from Canberra, Australia.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:37.036
He's a senior

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:37.670
analyst

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.272
with the Australian Strategic

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.074
Policy Institute.

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.842
Thank you so much for being here with us.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:46.179
So with this, you know, spy balloon

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:49.582
in some ways it seems comically low tech,

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.084
but what do you make of this balloon

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:53.519
and its purpose and capabilities?

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.023
Look, I think what it is is

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.858
certainly a political message

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.127
being sent by China

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.830
to challenge the US in terms of

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.098
the upcoming visit

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:07.300
by Secretary of State Blinken.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:08.401
You know,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.869
it's a bit of a provocative shot

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.670
across the US

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.171
because in that sense,

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.340
from a military technical perspective,

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:15.775
I think as you say,

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:19.112
it's a very low tech way of undertaking

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:20.847
intelligence gathering a comparison

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.682
to, say, spy satellites,

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:25.818
but in the way that they could use this

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:26.619
balloon to gather

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:27.887
signals intelligence

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.589
and electronic intelligence.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:30.957
They have a critical military site.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:32.558
It's probably

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.927
quite a provocative

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:35.661
but challenging

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.863
but effective

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:39.232
way of gathering intelligence.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.501
So so you think it's more to to sort of

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.903
listen in rather than to to see things?

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:44.871
I guess

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.740
the US decision not to shoot it down,

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.142
it surprised some people.

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:51.043
Do you agree with the rationale?

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.378
Just let it go?

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.615
Yes, essentially because

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:56.082
if you look

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:58.518
at the imagery of the balloon,

00:06:58.518 --> 00:06:58.951
you'll note

00:06:58.951 --> 00:06:59.752
that there's

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:03.356
two large areas of solar panels below it.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.123
And then

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:04.891
in the middle

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:07.860
there is a series of equipment

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.695
sections, essentially

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.697
an instrumentation package.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:12.598
This would have a fair

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:13.232
bit of mass

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.001
given the size of the balloon.

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:16.903
So if they shut the balloon down,

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:18.871
there's quite the possibility

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.573
that that instrumentation package

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:21.474
and the solar panels

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:23.609
could actually cause damage

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:24.277
or potentially

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.211
even harm people

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.846
on the surface below when it came

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:28.381
crashing down.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:28.681
Okay.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.783
But it has to come down sometime.

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.718
So where could it land?

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:33.820
And then what happens then?

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.455
Does it does it sort of

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.056
will we see a James Bond like

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:38.791
race to get to it first?

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:41.761
Well, my initial thought was

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.829
I station zebra,

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:44.430
if you remember that movie,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.398
but essentially, yes,

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.733
it does have to come down at some point.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.836
And so the instrumentation package

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.037
on that balloon

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:54.607
would be of intelligence value to the US

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:55.875
The US would obviously

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:57.343
want to get a hold of that.

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:58.911
The Chinese would want to stop them

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.079
from getting that.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:00.813
So it really does

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.048
depend on where it comes down.

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:03.749
If it comes down over the ocean,

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.785
perhaps in the Gulf of Mexico

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:08.454
or on the Atlantic Ocean,

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:09.489
then it is a challenge

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:11.524
in terms of recovering up from the water.

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:12.525
If it comes down over

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:15.061
land, potentially over Central America

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:16.229
or Mexico.

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.030
That's an even more challenging scenario

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:18.731
because then it's in

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:20.233
someone else's territory.

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:21.033
So it will be interesting

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.236
to see how that ultimate endgame

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:24.170
works out.

